[dvystrcil/gpu-batch] Investigate n8n-lane-a job failure in gpu-batch  (model=qwen3-coder-next:latest, 46s, lane=claude)
## Why
The `n8n-lane-a` job in the `gpu-batch` namespace is consistently ending in `Error`. This prevents the batch lane from processing CAD-to-printer jobs reliably, blocking the GPU batch lane's core function of fire-and-forget printing off the laptop.

## What we know
- The issue was flagged via KubeJobFailed alert firing in `gpu-batch` namespace ([https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1941](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1941)).
- The `gpu-batch` repo defines a CronJob-based trigger system; Jobs are created dynamically by `bin/gpu-batch-submit.py` from templates like `base/freecad-sweep.yaml`.
- The `n8n-lane-a` job is part of the chained workflow: FreeCAD → PrusaSlicer → Moonraker, orchestrated via n8n (see [https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1961](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1961)).
- A related open issue notes workflows in git and n8n disagree (rolling) ([https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1978](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1978)).

**unverified**: exact error message or pod logs — not present in provided context.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** `kubectl -n gpu-batch get jobs,nodes,pods -o wide` shows `n8n-lane-a-*` Job status as `Complete` (not `Error`) with all pods in `Running` or `Succeeded`.
- [ ] **AC2.** Running `bin/gpu-batch-submit.py --dry-run --lane n8n-lane-a` produces no Python exceptions and outputs a valid Job manifest.
- [ ] **AC3.** The compose test harness (`gpu-batch-docker/bin/compose-test.sh --lane n8n-lane-a`) passes without failure.

## Lane
claude — requires investigation of k8s Job logs, n8n workflow state, and potential mismatch between git-tracked manifests and live n8n configuration.

